// the fitted network is not an approximation of anything — it paints garbage —
// so the guard replaces it with a conservative sphere distance. This is NOT the
// same thing as bunnyBound() and cannot be folded into it: a bound only
// short-circuits when a ray is FAR, and the marcher still evaluates the real sdf
// once inside the bound's margin band. The guard is a precondition on the
// function; the bound is an accelerator. Both exist, deliberately.
